Blox Trade — Privacy Policy

Last Updated: November 17, 2026

Blox Trade respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how the extension accesses and uses information to provide its features.

1. Information Accessed

Blox Trade accesses the following information when necessary:

Roblox Username: To identify the account currently logged into your browser.

Roblox User ID: To identify your Roblox account.

Limited Inventory: To retrieve information about your Limited items.

Total Limited RAP: To calculate and display the combined RAP of your Limited inventory.

2. How Information Is Used

The information accessed by Blox Trade is used to provide its features directly to you, including:

Displaying your Roblox account information.

Calculating your total Limited RAP.

Displaying inventory statistics.

Providing trade calculations and related features.

Your inventory information is used locally by the extension to provide these features.

3. Data Storage

Blox Trade may store extension settings locally in your browser to remember your preferences.

Inventory information is accessed when needed for the extension's functionality.

4. Third-Party Services

Blox Trade interacts with Roblox to retrieve information necessary for its features.

Roblox is an independent third-party platform governed by its own Privacy Policy and Terms of Service.

Blox Trade is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or officially associated with Roblox Corporation.

